  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Brahmanand vs State Of U.P. And Another on 14 November, 2019 Author: Sudhir Agarwal Bench: Sudhir Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad Court No. - 34 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 2395 of 2000 Revisionist :- Brahmanand Opposite Party :- State of U.P. and Another Counsel for Revisionist :- K.M. Mishra, Anil Kumar Bajpai Counsel for Opposite Party :- Govt. Advocate Hon'ble Sudhir Agarwal,J. 1.",
    "facts": "This revision has been filed challenging both the aforesaid orders. 3. Learned counsel for revisionist contended that there was violation of Section 13(2) of Act, 1954 inasmuch report of Public Analyst was not served upon revisionist. * * \"P.W-2, R.S. Yadav, Food Inspector, has in his statement made mention of having sent the report by registered post to the accused on 18.03.1997.",
    "arguments": "However, I find that approach of Courts below with respect to compliance of Section 13(2) of Act is in the teeth of recent judgment of Supreme Court in Vijendra Vs. State of U.P. and others (Criminal Appeal No. 1167 of 2019) (Arising out of S.L.P. (Criminal) No. 4314 of 2015) decided on 31.07.2019 wherein Court in para 15 of judgment said as under: \"The very purpose of furnishing such report is to enable the Accused to seek for reference to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis if the Accused is dissatisfied with the report.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "However, I find that approach of Courts below with respect to compliance of Section 13(2) of Act is in the teeth of recent judgment of Supreme Court in Vijendra Vs. State of U.P. and others (Criminal Appeal No. 1167 of 2019) (Arising out of S.L.P. (Criminal) No. 4314 of 2015) decided on 31.07.2019 wherein Court in para 15 of judgment said as under: \"The very purpose of furnishing such report is to enable the Accused to seek for reference to the Central Food Laboratory for analysis if the Accused is dissatisfied with the report."
  },
